cntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)` and the refused attempt both route through the same module-level `fcntl`","gate_admission.py:270 release path calls `fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)` through the same proxy","existing test structure (test_gate_admission_09da.py:159-168): the refusal and the assert both sit INSIDE t-1's still-open `with ga.gate_admission('plan_review','t-1',root)` context, so t-1's acquire is already recorded before t-2 is attempted","plan phrase: 'the refused admission made exactly limit (1) lock attempts, each with LOCK_NB'"],"finding":"Mechanism 3's assertion of 'exactly limit (1) lock attempts' will not hold as written: at the assertion point the flock proxy has recorded both the holder t-1's acquire flock and the refused t-2's attempt (both LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB), so a global count sees 2 LOCK_NB attempts, not 1 (and the holder's LOCK_UN release also passes through the same ga.fcntl).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcdb07240e7c8de31","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 (test_the_refusal_returns_immediately_rather_than_waiting_for_a_holder)","norm_id":"n6c218a7ce30b6623","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running the rewritten test: assertion counts 2 LOCK_NB flock calls (t-1 acquire + t-2 refusal) and fails even on correct production code"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Record flock calls into a list and, immediately before entering the `with ga.gate_admission('plan_review','t-2',root)` refusal, snapshot/clear the list; then assert the refusal added exactly `limit` entries, each carrying LOCK_NB.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_